#description: A schema open to fields it does not declare. An instance may hold any other field beside the ones the schema declares, and a program reading the instance through the Go type sees the declared fields as the instance holds them.
#version: 0.0
#spec: docs/translation.md:44
#expect: ok
#known/cue/undeclared-differs-by-case: #303 Value decodes with CUE's Decode, which matches a key to a Go field whatever its case, so ID overwrites id.
#description/declared-only: Only the declared field.
#description/undeclared-field: A field the schema does not declare, beside the one it does.
#description/undeclared-differs-by-case: A field the schema does not declare, ID, whose name differs from the declared id only by case. id is still a.
-- open/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	...
}
-- data/declared-only.json --
{"id":"a"}
-- data/undeclared-field.json --
{"id":"a","color":"red"}
-- data/undeclared-differs-by-case.json --
{"id":"a","ID":"b"}
-- out/cue/declared-only --
verdict: ok
value: {"id":"a"}
-- out/cue/undeclared-differs-by-case --
verdict: wrong
the Go value is {"id":"b"}
the instance, decoded onto the type, is {"id":"a"}
-- out/cue/undeclared-field --
verdict: ok
value: {"id":"a"}
